    <string name="touch_live_bindings_hint" translatable="false">Racing touch buttons follow the game’s current control assignments, including gamepad buttons and axes. Menu controls use automatic defaults.</string>
    <string name="controls_automatic_note" translatable="false">Gamepads connect automatically. Set racing buttons and axes in the game’s Controls menu. On-screen racing buttons follow those assignments.</string>
    <string name="controls_automatic_help">Menus: use the D-pad or left stick to move, A / Cross to confirm, and B / Circle to go back. In Gamepads, you can test controllers and change their menu controls. Touch users can choose Direct touch or Touchpad in Touch controls.\n\nRacing: assign controls in the game’s Controls menu. On-screen racing buttons follow those assignments. If your menu Back button is assigned to racing, choose an extra button under Gamepads → Race pause shortcut. Hold both to pause.\n\nSplit screen: choose a controller for each player in Gamepads. Automatic uses the remaining controllers in connection order. A saved assignment stays reserved while its controller is disconnected. Touch racing controls operate player 1.</string>
